\f5 \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\'81\'9c	}
\f1 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Strengthen grassroots policy advocacy: amplify green businesses\'92 voices to in\uc0\u64258 uence incentives, procurement, and regulatory frameworks.\par


ul Key Takeaway\ulnone: Green economies grow fastest when government policy, public investment, and entrepreneurs move together. African BDS providers and SEED-stage green businesses should leverage policy windows, co-develop infrastructure, and use public capital to scale innovations effectively.\


\pard\tx1275\tx1730\pardeftab720\li1730\fi-1730\sa11\partightenfactor0
