\f6\i\b0 \cf6 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone 	3.1.1.\cf6 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Global Climate & Trade Frameworks: Enablers for Scalable Green Business\par

\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\fi1275\sa58\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\b \cf2 United Nations: SDGs & Paris Agreement: National Green Commitments\par

\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\ri1293\sa237\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 The global sustainability agenda, led by the UN\'92s SDGs and the Paris Agreement, has been instrumental in shaping African green markets. Most African countries have translated these frameworks into Nationally Determined Contributions (NDCs), which define emissions reduction targets and sectoral strategies. For green businesses, this has created clear demand signals in areas like renewable energy, water access, and sustainable agriculture.\par
\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\ri1292\sa159\qj\partightenfactor0

\f6\i \cf2 Why it matters for SEED/BDS providers: 
\f1\i0 National climate plans (e.g., Kenya\'92s 100% clean electricity goal by 2030 ) often come with investment plans, technical assistance, and policy changes (like feed-in tariffs or energy subsidies ) that green
\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\ri1291\sa241\qj\partightenfactor0\n\f1\b0 \cf2 businesses can tap into, especially if BDS providers help founders map these incentives.\
\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\fi1275\sa57\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 OECD & Global Policy Guidance 
\f8 \uc0\u8594 
\f0 Market Entry Blueprints\par

\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\ri1291\sa237\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 Though not African members, OECD\'92s green growth frameworks ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.oecd-ilibrary.org/en/about/programmes/oecd-platform-on-financing-smes-for-sustainability.html"}}{\fldrslt \cf7 \ul \ulc7 OECD Platform}}\cf7 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.oecd-ilibrary.org/en/about/programmes/oecd-platform-on-financing-smes-for-sustainability.html"}}{\fldrslt \cf7 \ul \ulc7 on Financing SMEs for Sustainability}}\cf2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.oecd-ilibrary.org/en/topics/greening-smes.html"}}{\fldrslt \cf7 \ul \ulc7 OECD \'96 Greening SMEs}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.oecd-ilibrary.org/en/topics/sustainable-finance.html"}}{\fldrslt \cf7 \ul \ulc7 OECD \'96 Guidance on}}\cf7 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.oecd-ilibrary.org/en/topics/sustainable-finance.html"}}{\fldrslt \cf7 \ul \ulc7 Transition Finance}}\cf2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.oecd-ilibrary.org/en/topics/sustainable-finance.html"}}{\fldrslt \cf7 \ul \ulc7 OECD \'96 Sustainable Finance}}, \'85 ) shape donor priorities and in\uc0\u64258 uence national policies. Its guidance on green job metrics, climate-smart public procurement, and sustainable finance standards gives BDS providers tools to align green businesses impact metrics with investor and donor expectations.\par
\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\ri1289\sa234\qj\partightenfactor0

\f6\i \cf2 Green businesses takeaway: 
\f1\i0 For example, when Senegal applied OECD-aligned green procurement rules, local solar companies gained priority in tenders. BDS providers can help green businesses certify as \'93green-compliant\'94 to unlock procurement or blended finance opportunities.\par
\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\fi1275\sa59\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 WTO and Trade Mechanisms; Lowering Costs & Expanding Markets\par

\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\ri1289\sa237\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 Trade policies can be powerful enablers. In countries that waived VAT/import duties on solar (e.g., Kenya, Tanzania), solar kit prices dropped 24%, boosting green businesses revenue by ~25%.\par
\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\ri1294\sa2\qj\partightenfactor0

\f6\i \cf2 For SEED ventures: 
\f1\i0 Trade-enabling frameworks (like the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wto.org/english/tratop_e/envir_e/ega_e.htm"}}{\fldrslt \cf7 \ul \ulc7 Environmental Goods}}\cf7 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wto.org/english/tratop_e/envir_e/ega_e.htm"}}{\fldrslt \cf7 \ul \ulc7 Agreement}} \cf2 or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://africanlii.org/fr/akn/aa-au/act/protocol/2023/free_trade_area_on_investment/eng@2023-02-19"}}{\fldrslt \cf7 \ul \ulc7 AfCFTA\'92s green investment rules}}) mean faster market expansion, lower cost of goods, and less red tape. BDS providers should advocate for harmonized customs rules and co-develop regional distribution playbooks with founders.\par

\pard\tx1275\tx1828\pardeftab720\li1828\fi-1828\sa55\partightenfactor0
\ls50\ilvl2
\f6\i \cf5 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone 	3.1.2.\cf5 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone African Frameworks: Scaling Through Integration and Innovation\par

\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\fi1275\sa58\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\b \cf2 AU Agenda 2063 
\f8 \uc0\u8594 
\f0 Pan-African Vision, Local Opportunity\par

\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\ri1291\sa236\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 Agenda 2063 sees green growth as central to Africa\'92s transformation, with targets for renewables, reforestation, and green jobs. It gives legitimacy to national climate goals and fosters competition among states to show progress.\par
\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\ri1292\sa159\qj\partightenfactor0

\f6\i \cf2 For green businesses/BDS providers: 
\f1\i0 Use this framework to argue for anchor government support, e.g., accessing grants under Green Job strategies, or forming
\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\ri1291\sa241\qj\partightenfactor0\n\f1\b0 \cf2 coalitions around agroecology, green building, or cleantech green businesses that deliver Agenda 2063 milestones.\
\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\fi1275\sa58\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 AfCFTA: From Trade Agreement to Green businesses Accelerator\par

\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\ri1290\sa237\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 The African Continental Free Trade Area (AfCFTA ) is Africa\'92s single biggest market integration move, covering 54 countries. Its 2023 Investment Protocol adds sustainability criteria to cross-border business. Future environmental protocols could add tax harmonization or emissions standards.\par
\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\ri1296\sa234\qj\partightenfactor0

\f6\i \cf2 Green businesses impact: 
\f1\i0 AfCFTA makes it easier to scale regionally, e.g., a PAYG solar firm from Kenya can enter Togo or Benin without navigating dozens of tax or customs systems. BDS providers can train founders on cross-border compliance and design playbooks to leverage AfCFTA\'92s mutual recognition clauses for things like clean energy appliances or green certification.\par
\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\fi1275\sa59\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 AGSP & Green Recovery Action Plan: The green businesses-Ready Policy Layer\par

\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\ri1293\sa5\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 Born post-COVID, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://agsp.nepad.org/"}}{\fldrslt \cf7 \ul \ulc7 African Green Stimulus Programme}}\cf7 \ul \ulc7 \cf2 \ulnone (AGSP ) emphasizes green entrepreneurship, youth and women-led ventures, and post-pandemic recovery through green jobs.\par

\pard\tx1275\tx1826\pardeftab720\li1826\fi-1826\sa55\partightenfactor0
\ls51\ilvl2
\f6\i \cf5 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone 	3.1.3.\cf5 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Finance-Driving Policy Structures: Unlocking Capital Through Reform\par

\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\fi1275\sa58\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\b \cf2 AfDB and Climate Finance Ecosystem Builders\par

\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\ri1291\sa237\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 The African Development Bank (AfDB ) is not just a funder, it\'92s a policy reform in\uc0\u64258 uencer. Its programs, like the African Green Bank Initiative and climate guarantee schemes, de-risk early-stage green businesses and push countries to develop green credit lines.\par
\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\ri1291\sa3\qj\partightenfactor0

\f6\i \cf2 Green businesses ecosystem value: 
\f1\i0 When AfDB guarantees solar programs in Togo or helps Kenya revise energy policies, it opens up local banks to lend, reduces risk for VCs, and often introduces tech assistance programs (like grid regulation or carbon MRV systems). BDS providers can connect founders to AfDB-backed guarantee schemes or concessional finance lines for RE, EV, circularity, and agri innovations.\par

\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\fi1275\sa3\partightenfactor0

