\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\ri1293\sa46\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 A Frontier Market for Decentralized Energy, Circular Economy, and Climate-Smart AgriTech\par

\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\fi1275\sa89\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 Country Snapshot\par

\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\sa47\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 Togo\'92s growing population (9.5M in 2025 ) and fast-paced urbanization (Lom\'e9\par
\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\ri1291\sa241\qj\partightenfactor0\n\f1\b0 \cf2 >1.5M ) make it an increasingly important green market in West Africa. While 40% of GDP comes from agriculture and 70% of the population is rural, Togo is betting on renewable energy, sustainable farming, and recycling to reshape its development model. The green economy already contributes to 12.7% of formal employment, with solar and waste management taking the lead.\

\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\fi1275\sa59\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 Green Market Opportunities for green businesses\par

\pard\tx1635\tx1995\pardeftab720\li1995\fi-1995\sa90\partightenfactor0
\ls160\ilvl0
\f3 \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	1.	}
\f0 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Waste Management & Circular Economy\par

\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\ri1292\sa48\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 Lom\'e9 generates 1,000+ tons/day of waste, with few formalized recycling systems. This has opened the door for early movers like Plastic Odyssey, which turns LDPE waste into construction material. Other active models consist of the following:\par

\pard\tx1635\tx1995\pardeftab720\li1995\fi-1995\sa43\partightenfactor0
\ls161\ilvl1
\f5 \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\'81\'9c	}
\f1 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Plastic-to-fuel and recycled furniture (pilot-tested)\par
\ls161\ilvl1
\f5 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\'81\'9c	}
\f1 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Eco-box collection services (small but scalable)\par
\pard\tx1635\tx1995\pardeftab720\li1995\fi-1995\ri1303\sa48\partightenfactor0
\ls161\ilvl1
\f5 \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\'81\'9c	}
\f1 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Replicable micro-factory models that could be franchised across other municipalities\par

\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\ri1291\sa241\qj\partightenfactor0\n\f1\b0 \cf2 Recycling is expected to become more formalized under the Circular Economy 2030 Plan, offering opportunities for green businesses in plastics, e-waste, and composting.\

\pard\tx1635\tx1994\tx1994\pardeftab720\li1994\fi-1994\sa90\partightenfactor0
\ls162\ilvl0
\f3\b \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	2.	}
\f0 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Renewable Energy & Rural Electrification\par

\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\ri1290\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 Togo offers one of West Africa\'92s most structured and ambitious rural electrification roadmaps. Programs like CIZO and Tinga use subsidies and pay-as-you-go (PAYG ) models to expand solar home systems and mini-grids. Key opportunities for SEED-stage green businesses include:\page 

\pard\tx1635\tx1995\pardeftab720\li1995\fi-1995\sa43\partightenfactor0
\ls163\ilvl1
\f5 \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\'81\'9c	}
\f1 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone SHS and productive-use appliances (e.g. solar fridges, pumps)\par
\ls163\ilvl1
\f5 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\'81\'9c	}
\f1 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Battery storage and smart metering innovations\par
\pard\tx1635\tx1995\pardeftab720\li1995\fi-1995\sa94\partightenfactor0
\ls163\ilvl1
\f5 \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\'81\'9c	}
\f1 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Rural e-mobility powered by solar charging\par

\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\ri1291\sa241\qj\partightenfactor0\n\f1\b0 \cf2 Flagship projects like the Sokod\'e9 62 MW plant and the Benban-style Dapaong solar + storage project show a public-private appetite for integrated solar systems. Foreign green businesses like M-KOPA and Qotto are already scaling, showing that partnerships with donors or distribution networks are key to growth.\

\pard\tx1635\tx1994\tx1994\pardeftab720\li1994\fi-1994\sa11\partightenfactor0
\ls164\ilvl0
\f3\b \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	3.	}
\f0 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Climate-Smart Agriculture\par

\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\ri1297\sa240\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 Togo\'92s agri sector employs over 60% of the population, and the country is actively transitioning to drought-resistant, tech-enabled farming. Opportunities for green businesses consist of the following:\par
\pard\tx1635\tx1995\pardeftab720\li1995\fi-1995\sa43\partightenfactor0
\ls165\ilvl1
\f5 \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\'81\'9c	}
\f1 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Drip irrigation with mobile microfinance\par
\ls165\ilvl1
\f5 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\'81\'9c	}
\f1 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Blockchain-powered traceability for cocoa, cotton\par
\pard\tx1635\tx1995\pardeftab720\li1995\fi-1995\sa15\partightenfactor0
\ls165\ilvl1
\f5 \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\'81\'9c	}
\f1 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone IoT or sensor-enabled field monitoring\par

\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\ri1291\sa241\qj\partightenfactor0\n\f1\b0 \cf2 Government-backed initiatives like the Eco-Village program and IoT-enabled irrigation pilots (NDC Plan ) signal openness to agri-tech innovation, though affordability remains a challenge.\

\pard\pardeftab720\li1337\sa178\qj\partightenfactor0

