\f0\b \cf2 Strategic Takeaway: Expansion Potential\par

\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\ri1289\sa240\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 Senegal stands out as a policy-advanced, investor-ready gateway for green green businesses entering the Francophone West African market. The presence of large-scale renewable projects, circular waste initiatives in Dakar, and digitized agricultural value chains makes Senegal especially attractive for green businesses scaling in clean energy, mobility, agri-tech, and digital waste management.\par
\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\ri1291\sa241\qj\partightenfactor0\n\f1\b0 \cf2 Regional green businesses offering mini-grid services, solar logistics platforms, IoT-based agri tools, or plastic valorization models can find a favorable environment supported by national plans and IPP-friendly regulation.\
\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\ri1291\sa241\qj\partightenfactor0\n\f1\b0 \cf2 To support green businesses expanding into Senegal, BDS providers should:\

\pard\tx1635\tx1995\pardeftab720\li1995\fi-1995\sa91\partightenfactor0
\ls216\ilvl1
