\f0\b \cf2 Fact sheet - Kenya\par

\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\fi1275\ri1288\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf2 East Africa\'92s Green Powerhouse: Leading in Geothermal, Solar Irrigation, and Electric Mobility\par
\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\ri1291\sa241\qj\partightenfactor0\n\f1\b0 \cf2 Country Snapshot\

\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\ri1289\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 Kenya stands out as one of Africa\'92s green champions. With a population of over 54 million and a GDP of $120 billion (2024), the economy is growing steadily at 5\'966% per year. Notably, the country boasts a ~90% renewable energy mix, anchored in geothermal (44% of electricity), with growing solar and wind capacity. Green sectors already account for a significant share of employment, and Nairobi has become a continental hub for clean-tech green businesses and climate finance. According to Florent Nduwayezu (FP Capital), the maturity level of Kenya\'92s green industry remains low. He rated it 1 out of 5, emphasizing that despite some activity, structural weaknesses (infrastructure, research, and talent ) limit scalability across most green sectors.\par


\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\fi1275\sa58\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 Green Market Opportunities for green businesses\par

\pard\tx1275\tx1474\pardeftab720\li1474\fi-1474\sa63\partightenfactor0
\ls217\ilvl0
\f2\b0 \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone 	1.
\f1 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Renewable Energy and Off-grid Solutions\par

\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\ri1291\sa241\qj\partightenfactor0\n\f1\b0 \cf2 Kenya is the 6th largest geothermal producer in the world and East Africa\'92s solar leader, with 985 MW of geothermal, 600 MW of wind, and 300 MW of solar installed. Projects like Lake Turkana (310 MW ) and the Garissa Solar Park (54 MW ) re\uc0\u64258 ect sustained public-private collaboration.\
\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\sa59\qj\partightenfactor0
