\fs24 \cf2 \par
\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\ri1291\sa241\qj\partightenfactor0\n\f1\b0 \cf2 Despite over a decade of programming, many green green businesses in South Africa still cycle through multiple support initiatives (e.g., one entrepreneur in Mpumalanga had completed 11 programs without accessing funding). This highlights the fragmented and ineffective structure of current ecosystem support models, particularly outside major urban hubs.\

\pard\pardeftab720\li1275\ri1288\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Nick Allen, the Managing Director of Savant, emphasizes that product-market fit remains the top barrier. He explained the di
culty green businesses face in gaining traction due to a market preference for \'93proven\'94 solutions. He shared examples, such as biogas projects that failed due to user hesitancy despite being fully funded. This ties into the broader challenge of building trust and credibility in new tech, which also hampers access to commercial funding without a proven track record.\par


